#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
"""Build one target: preflight, the exports, their checks, materialization and the build
record (specs/001-base-build, FR-001, FR-004). Writes into the artifacts folder and
nowhere else (docs/artifacts.md).

    scripts/build TARGET [OPTIONS]

  TARGET  a directory under targets/ (its target file names the arch); the base is the
          chain ending in device-<TARGET>, DEVICE=TARGET for every stage

Options:
  --artifacts DIR      the artifacts folder (default: artifacts/ in this checkout,
                       git-ignored); created if missing
  --parent BASE_ID     the parent of a new base (default: the base of the newest build
                       record of TARGET in the artifacts folder)
  --no-parent          a new base gets no parent
  --build-arg N=V      a build argument for every stage (repeat); must be an ARG of the
                       Dockerfile; a value other than its default (or any value of one
                       without a default, such as JOBS) makes the build a trial. DEVICE
                       is the target and can't be set
  --local NAME=DIR     build a git input from a local checkout instead of its pinned
                       source (repeat, one per repository): NAME is the input's commit
                       ARG (LINUX_SDM660, DTB_COMMIT, BOOT_COMMIT) or its repository's
                       ARG (LINUX, BOOT); either way every input of that repository
                       comes from DIR. The input NAME names is DIR's HEAD (its
                       --build-arg can't be set too); every other input of the
                       repository is DIR's HEAD as well (DTB_COMMIT moves with a kernel
                       checkout), unless a --build-arg sets it apart, which then names
                       a commit DIR has. The build is a trial (local:<input>)
  --no-cache           build every stage without BuildKit's layer cache, once per run
                       (an export reuses what an earlier export of this run built);
                       cache mounts, such as the kernel's, are kept: an empty one gives
                       the same bytes
  --preflight-only     run the preflight, print the build info it found, stop

In order (each step's time is printed, and again at the end):
  1. preflight (below); any failure ends the command before a stage builds, naming each
     cause
  2. local checkouts (--local): each input's commit fetched from DIR into a fresh
     checkout in the work directory, shallow like the pinned source, given to every
     export as the source stage's build context (docker buildx --build-context
     <stage>=<dir>), so the Dockerfile is the same for every build
  3. the exports, docker buildx for linux/<arch>: base-export as a tar, kernel-export,
     dtb-export, initramfs-export and boot-export as local directories merged into one
  4. scripts/kernel-check and scripts/boot-check on the merged directory (boot-check
     with --cmdline-extra when CMDLINE_EXTRA is set)
  5. scripts/materialize with the overrides (--arg), the build info (--build-info), the
     parent options and the build's start (--time)

Preflight (FR-004), in seconds, all checks run and every failure is named (an error
inside a check is that check's failure):
  - docker, git and python3 present; the target's file; the overrides are ARGs of the
    Dockerfile; the target's kernel= is the effective KERNEL (the Dockerfile's KERNEL is
    a pin: a target on another kernel needs its own, or a --build-arg trial)
  - every stage the exports build from that installs packages (stages/<stage>/packages)
    has its lock; the base chain starts from an image, not from a missing stage
  - the parent: the named base, or the base of the newest build record, is complete
    (record, content manifest, streams matching their sha256)
  - emulation: every platform the build needs (linux/<arch> and each constant
    FROM --platform= in the Dockerfile) that isn't the host's is listed by docker buildx
  - a privileged container can attach a loop device to a file on a tmpfs, and the
    kernel has btrfs loaded (what materialization does); it runs MATERIALIZE_IMAGE, so that image is pullable too
  - free space: 2 GiB in the artifacts folder (a build stages the tar export, ~0.5 GiB,
    and the kernel exports, ~0.1 GiB, next to the streams it writes: the full stream
    ~0.2 GiB, the modules stream ~25 MiB), 10 GiB for the docker root (the kernel's
    cache mount alone holds ~7.5 GiB, plus the stage layers); 12 GiB when both are on
    one file system (taken as one when both report the same size and free space
    within 256 MiB). The docker root's space is what the probe container sees (the
    daemon's own view, also for a remote daemon); DockerRootDir on this host only when
    the probe gives none.
    BUILD_MIN_ARTIFACTS_GIB and BUILD_MIN_DOCKER_GIB change the thresholds
  - every git input's commit (its "# branch:" ARG, with the overrides) can be fetched
    from its repository (the URL ARG declared beside it): a shallow, treeless fetch of
    the commit into a throwaway bare repository, which also gives its tree
  - each --local DIR: a directory at the top of a git checkout, with no uncommitted
    changes (tracked files, and untracked files git doesn't ignore: the same rule as
    this checkout's); a checkout of the input's repository: it has one of the
    repository's pinned commits, or a remote with the repository's URL; each commit set
    apart by a --build-arg is a commit of DIR. Its commit's tree is the input's tree; the
    commit is fetched from the repository as above to decide unmerged, and one the
    repository doesn't have (not pushed) is unmerged. The free space needed in the
    artifacts folder grows by one and a half times the size of each checkout's files
  - every builder image pinned by digest (<X>_IMAGE + <X>_DIGEST) and the base image
    (ALPINE) can be pulled (docker buildx imagetools inspect)

Build info for materialize: images_commit (git rev-parse HEAD) and images_clean (the
checkout's tracked files and the untracked files git doesn't ignore, which a stage's COPY
reads, are HEAD's tree), both taken at preflight and taken again after the exports: a
change in between fails the build, input.<ARG>.tree (the fetched commit's tree),
input.<ARG>.local (yes for an input from --local DIR), builder.<image> = its pinned digest, and unmerged: the inputs
whose commit isn't an ancestor of their branch's tip. For a github.com repository that
is the compare API (one request: compare/<commit>...<branch> is "ahead" or "identical"
when the commit is on the branch; GITHUB_TOKEN or GH_TOKEN is used when set). Elsewhere,
or when the API doesn't answer: the branch is fetched treeless back to a day before the
commit's date and git merge-base --is-ancestor decides; when that says no while history
was cut, the branch is unshallowed (bounded by a timeout) and asked again; still
undecided counts as unmerged.

Work files (the tar export, the kernel exports, the throwaway repositories, the local
checkouts' copies) live in <artifacts>/.work-<pid>/, a name never read as an artifact, removed at the
end, also on SIGTERM, SIGHUP and Ctrl-C (the running build step is stopped first); a
.work-<pid> whose process is gone is removed by the next run. The log of every run is
kept as <artifacts>/.logs/<TARGET>/<start>.log.

Environment: BUILD_TIMEOUT (seconds per export, default 14400), BUILD_MIN_ARTIFACTS_GIB,
BUILD_MIN_DOCKER_GIB, MATERIALIZE_IMAGE (default alpine:3.24), and materialize's own.

Exit: 0 built, 1 failed (nothing new in the artifacts folder but the log), 2 usage,
3 preflight failed, 4 another materialization holds the host lock.
"""
import concurrent.futures, contextlib, datetime, http.client, io, importlib.machinery
import importlib.util, json, os, platform, re, selectors, shutil, signal, subprocess, sys, time
import urllib.error, urllib.request

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
REPO = os.path.dirname(HERE)
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
import glassine_pins  # noqa: E402

_loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader('materialize', os.path.join(HERE, 'materialize'))
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader('materialize', _loader)
materialize = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
_loader.exec_module(materialize)

# The exports of a target, in build order: the base's tree, then the kernel side.
BASE_EXPORT = glassine_pins.BASE_STAGE
KERNEL_EXPORTS = ['kernel-export', 'dtb-export', 'initramfs-export', 'boot-export']
GIB = 1 << 30
ARCHES = {'x86_64': 'amd64', 'amd64': 'amd64', 'aarch64': 'arm64', 'arm64': 'arm64',
          'armv7l': 'arm', 'riscv64': 'riscv64', 'ppc64le': 'ppc64le', 's390x': 's390x'}


class Fail(Exception):
    pass


def usage():
    print(__doc__, file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)


def parse(argv):
    o = {'artifacts': os.path.join(REPO, 'artifacts'), 'parent': None, 'no_parent': False,
         'args': {}, 'local': {}, 'no_cache': False, 'preflight_only': False}
    pos = []
    it = iter(argv)
    for a in it:
        if a in ('--artifacts', '--parent', '--build-arg', '--local'):
            v = next(it, None)
            if v is None:
                usage()
            if a in ('--build-arg', '--local'):
                k, sep, val = v.partition('=')
                if not sep or not re.fullmatch(r'\w+', k) or (a == '--local' and (not val or k in o['local'])):
                    usage()
                o['args' if a == '--build-arg' else 'local'][k] = val
            else:
                o[a[2:]] = v
        elif a in ('--no-parent', '--no-cache', '--preflight-only'):
            o[a[2:].replace('-', '_')] = True
        elif a in ('-h', '--help') or a.startswith('-'):
            usage()
        else:
            pos.append(a)
    if len(pos) != 1 or (o['parent'] and o['no_parent']):
        usage()
    return o, pos[0]


def run(cmd, timeout, **kw):
    """subprocess.run with a timeout; (returncode, stdout, stderr), 124 on timeout."""
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, errors='replace',
                           timeout=timeout, **kw)
        return p.returncode, p.stdout, p.stderr
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return 124, '', f'timed out after {timeout} s'
    except OSError as e:
        return 127, '', str(e)


def last(text):
    lines = [x for x in text.strip().splitlines() if x.strip()]
    return lines[-1].strip() if lines else ''


# ---- preflight ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def free_bytes(path):
    """(bytes free, file system size) for path or its nearest existing ancestor."""
    while not os.path.exists(path):
        path = os.path.dirname(path)
    st = os.statvfs(path)
    return st.f_bavail * st.f_frsize, st.f_blocks * st.f_frsize


def check_emulation(arch, others=()):
    """Every platform the build needs (the target's, linux/<arch>, and the constant
    --platform of any stage) that isn't the host's must be listed by docker buildx."""
    host = 'linux/' + ARCHES.get(platform.machine(), platform.machine())
    need = sorted(({f'linux/{arch}'} | set(others)) - {host})
    if not need:
        return []
    rc, out, err = run(['docker', 'buildx', 'inspect'], 30)
    if rc != 0:
        return [f'docker buildx inspect failed: {last(err) or last(out)}']
    plats = set()
    for line in out.splitlines():
        if line.strip().startswith('Platforms:'):
            plats |= {p.strip().rstrip('*') for p in line.split(':', 1)[1].split(',')}
    return [f'no emulation for {p} on this {host} host: docker buildx lists '
            f'{", ".join(sorted(plats)) or "no platforms"} (install QEMU user emulation with '
            f'binfmt_misc, e.g. the tonistiigi/binfmt image)' for p in need if p not in plats]


PROBE = r'''
set -e
for i in $(seq 0 31); do [ -e /dev/loop$i ] || mknod /dev/loop$i b 7 $i 2>/dev/null || true; done
mkdir -p /probe && mount -t tmpfs -o size=16m tmpfs /probe || { echo "probe: no tmpfs mount"; exit 3; }
truncate -s 8M /probe/f
l=$(losetup -f) || { echo "probe: no free loop device"; exit 3; }
losetup "$l" /probe/f || { echo "probe: losetup $l failed"; exit 3; }
losetup -d "$l"
grep -qw btrfs /proc/filesystems || { echo "probe: the kernel has no btrfs loaded (sudo modprobe btrfs)"; exit 3; }
echo "probe: df $(df -Pk / | tail -n 1 | awk '{print $2, $4}')"
'''


def check_privileged(image):
    """A privileged container attaches a loop device; returns (failures, docker root
    (free, size) as the container's / sees it, or None)."""
    rc, out, err = run(['docker', 'run', '--rm', '--privileged', image, 'sh', '-c', PROBE], 120)
    m = re.search(r'^probe: df (\d+) (\d+)$', out, re.M)
    if rc != 0:
        why = last(out) if last(out).startswith('probe:') else (last(err) or last(out))
        return [f'privileged container with loop devices failed ({image}): {why}'], None
    if not m:
        return [], None
    return [], (int(m.group(2)) * 1024, int(m.group(1)) * 1024)


def threshold(name, default):
    v = os.environ.get(name, str(default))
    try:
        x = float(v)
    except ValueError:
        x = -1
    if not x >= 0:
        raise Fail(f'{name}={v!r}: not a number of GiB')
    return x * GIB


def check_space(adir, docker_df, extra=0):
    """The artifacts folder's file system, and the docker root's as the daemon sees it:
    the probe's answer from inside a container (right for a remote daemon too); a local
    walk to DockerRootDir only when the probe gave none. extra: bytes the artifacts
    folder needs besides its threshold (the local checkouts' copies)."""
    fails = []
    need_a = threshold('BUILD_MIN_ARTIFACTS_GIB', 2) + extra
    need_d = threshold('BUILD_MIN_DOCKER_GIB', 10)
    a = free_bytes(adir)
    d = docker_df
    if d is None:
        rc, out, _ = run(['docker', 'info', '--format', '{{.DockerRootDir}}'], 30)
        root = out.strip() if rc == 0 else ''
        if root.startswith('/') and os.path.exists(root):
            try:
                d = free_bytes(root)
            except OSError:
                d = None
    if d is None:
        return ['free space of the docker root unknown (docker info and the probe gave none)']
    one = a[1] == d[1] and abs(a[0] - d[0]) < (256 << 20)
    for what, have, need in ([('the artifacts folder and the docker root (one file system)', a[0], need_a + need_d)]
                             if one else
                             [('the artifacts folder', a[0], need_a), ('the docker root', d[0], need_d)]):
        if have < need:
            fails.append(f'not enough free space for {what}: {have / GIB:.1f} GiB free, '
                         f'{need / GIB:.1f} GiB needed')
    return fails


def github(url):
    m = re.fullmatch(r'https://github\.com/([^/]+)/([^/]+?)(?:\.git)?/?', url)
    return m.groups() if m else None


def gh_merged(url, commit, branch):
    """True/False from GitHub's compare API, None when it doesn't answer."""
    owner_repo = github(url)
    if not owner_repo:
        return None
    req = urllib.request.Request(
        f'https://api.github.com/repos/{owner_repo[0]}/{owner_repo[1]}/compare/{commit}...'
        f'{urllib.request.quote(branch, safe="/")}?per_page=1',
        headers={'Accept': 'application/vnd.github+json'})
    tok = os.environ.get('GITHUB_TOKEN') or os.environ.get('GH_TOKEN')
    if tok:
        req.add_header('Authorization', f'Bearer {tok}')
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20) as r:
            status = json.load(r).get('status')
    except (urllib.error.URLError, http.client.HTTPException, OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not isinstance(status, str):
        return None
    return {'ahead': True, 'identical': True, 'behind': False, 'diverged': False}.get(status)


def git_merged(g, url, commit, branch, log):
    """Is commit an ancestor of branch's tip? From a treeless fetch of the branch back to
    a day before the commit's date; unshallowed when that says no (bounded)."""
    rc, out, _ = g('show', '-s', '--format=%ct', commit)
    since = int(out.strip()) - 86400 if rc == 0 and out.strip().isdigit() else 0
    ref = f'refs/heads/{branch}'
    rc, _, err = g('fetch', '-q', '--filter=tree:0', f'--shallow-since={since}', url,
                   f'+{ref}:{ref}', timeout=120)
    if rc != 0:     # nothing after that date: the tip alone
        rc, _, err = g('fetch', '-q', '--filter=tree:0', '--depth=1', url, f'+{ref}:{ref}', timeout=120)
        if rc != 0:
            raise Fail(f'branch {branch} can\'t be fetched from {url}: {last(err)}')
    if g('merge-base', '--is-ancestor', commit, ref)[0] == 0:
        return True
    rc, out, _ = g('rev-parse', '--is-shallow-repository')
    if out.strip() == 'true':
        log(f'preflight: {url} {branch}: history cut, unshallowing to decide')
        rc, _, err = g('fetch', '-q', '--filter=tree:0', '--unshallow', url, f'+{ref}:{ref}', timeout=240)
        if rc != 0:
            log(f'preflight: {url} {branch}: undecided ({last(err)}), counted as unmerged')
            return False
        return g('merge-base', '--is-ancestor', commit, ref)[0] == 0
    return False


def check_git(work, n, url, commit, branches, log, missing_ok=False):
    """Fetch commit (shallow, treeless) into a throwaway bare repository: its tree and,
    per branch, whether it is on it. Returns (failures, tree, {branch: merged}); a
    failure is a message, or (branch, message) when only that branch's inputs fail.
    missing_ok (a local checkout's commit): a commit the repository doesn't give is no
    failure but ([], None, {}), on no branch (not pushed)."""
    d = os.path.join(work, 'git', str(n))
    os.makedirs(d)

    def g(*a, timeout=60):
        return run(['git', '-C', d, '-c', 'protocol.version=2', *a], timeout,
                   env={**os.environ, 'GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT': '0'})
    g('init', '-q', '--bare')
    if not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{40}|[0-9a-f]{64}', commit):
        return [f'{commit!r} from {url} is not a full commit id'], '', {}
    rc, _, err = g('fetch', '-q', '--depth=1', '--filter=tree:0', url, commit)
    if rc != 0 and missing_ok:
        log(f'preflight: commit {commit} not in {url} ({last(err)}): not pushed, unmerged')
        return [], None, {}
    if rc != 0:
        return [f'commit {commit} not reachable in {url}: {last(err)}'], '', {}
    rc, tree, err = g('rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', f'{commit}^{{tree}}')
    if rc != 0:
        return [f'commit {commit} from {url}: no tree ({last(err)})'], '', {}
    merged, fails = {}, []
    for b in branches:
        m = gh_merged(url, commit, b)
        if m is None:
            try:
                m = git_merged(g, url, commit, b, log)
            except Fail as e:
                fails.append((b, str(e)))
                continue
        merged[b] = m
    return fails, tree.strip(), merged


def check_image(ref):
    rc, out, err = run(['docker', 'buildx', 'imagetools', 'inspect', ref], 60)
    if rc != 0:
        return [f'image {ref} not pullable: {last(err) or last(out)}']
    return []


def same_url(a, b):
    """Two repository URLs naming the same repository: host and path compared without a
    trailing / or .git, scp-like git@host:path read as host/path, file:// and plain
    paths by their real path."""
    def norm(u):
        u = u.strip()
        m = re.fullmatch(r'[\w.-]+@([\w.-]+):(?!//)(.+)', u)
        if m:
            u = f'ssh://{m.group(1)}/{m.group(2)}'
        if u.startswith('file://') or u.startswith('/'):
            return 'file:' + os.path.realpath(u[7:] if u.startswith('file://') else u).rstrip('/')
        m = re.fullmatch(r'[a-z+]+://(?:[^@/]+@)?([^/:]+)(?::\d+)?/(.+?)(?:\.git)?/*', u)
        return f'{m.group(1).lower()}/{m.group(2)}' if m else u
    return norm(a) == norm(b)


def local_inputs(dockerfile, local, over):
    """--local NAME=DIR: (failures, {input: facts}, covered) for every input of each
    named repository: dir, commit, tree, url, stage and path (its source stage), size
    (bytes of the commit's files); covered: every input of a named repository, also
    when its checkout failed a check. over: the overrides without the local commits."""
    fails, out, covered = [], {}, set()
    branches = glassine_pins.branches(dockerfile)
    rep = glassine_pins.repos(dockerfile)
    src = glassine_pins.sources(dockerfile)
    args, _ = glassine_pins.pins(dockerfile, over)
    claimed = {}
    for name, d0 in local.items():
        if name in branches:
            repo_arg, named = rep[name], name
        elif name in rep.values():
            repo_arg, named = name, None
        else:
            fails.append(f'--local {name}: not a git input or the ARG of its repository '
                         f'(one of {", ".join(sorted(set(branches) | set(rep.values())))})')
            continue
        if repo_arg in claimed:
            fails.append(f'--local {name}: its repository ({repo_arg}) is already --local {claimed[repo_arg]}')
            continue
        claimed[repo_arg] = name
        members = [i for i in branches if rep[i] == repo_arg]
        covered |= set(members)
        if named and named in over:
            fails.append(f'--local {named}: the checkout gives its commit; --build-arg {named} can\'t be set too')
            continue
        what = f'--local {name}={d0}'
        d = os.path.realpath(d0)
        if not os.path.isdir(d):
            fails.append(f'{what}: no such directory')
            continue

        def g(*a, timeout=60):
            return run(['git', '-C', d, *a], timeout, env={**os.environ, 'GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT': '0'})
        rc, top, err = g('rev-parse', '--show-toplevel')
        if rc != 0:
            fails.append(f'{what}: not a git checkout ({last(err)})')
            continue
        if os.path.realpath(top.strip()) != d:
            fails.append(f'{what}: not the top of its git checkout ({top.strip()})')
            continue
        rc, head, _ = g('rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', 'HEAD^{commit}')
        if rc != 0:
            fails.append(f'{what}: no commit checked out')
            continue
        head = head.strip()
        rc, st, err = g('status', '--porcelain', '--untracked-files=normal', timeout=300)
        if rc != 0:
            fails.append(f'{what}: git status failed ({last(err)})')
            continue
        if st.strip():
            changed = [x for x in st.splitlines() if x.strip()]
            fails.append(f'{what}: uncommitted changes, {len(changed)} path(s) '
                         f'({", ".join(x[3:] for x in changed[:3])}{", ..." if len(changed) > 3 else ""}); '
                         'commit or stash them (a local checkout must be clean)')
            continue
        url = args.get(repo_arg, '')
        pinned = sorted({args.get(i, '') for i in members} - {''})
        has_pin = any(g('cat-file', '-e', f'{c}^{{commit}}')[0] == 0 for c in pinned)
        rc, remotes, _ = g('remote', '-v')
        has_remote = any(same_url(line.split()[1], url) for line in remotes.splitlines()
                         if len(line.split()) >= 2)
        if not (has_pin or has_remote):
            fails.append(f'{what}: not a checkout of {url} ({repo_arg}): it has none of its pinned '
                         f'commits ({", ".join(c[:12] for c in pinned)}) and no remote with that URL')
            continue
        for i in members:
            commit = head
            if i in over and i != named:
                rc, c, _ = g('rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', f'{over[i]}^{{commit}}')
                if rc != 0:
                    fails.append(f'--build-arg {i}={over[i]}: not a commit of the local checkout '
                                 f'of {repo_arg} (fetch it into {d0})')
                    continue
                commit = c.strip()
            rc, tree, _ = g('rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', f'{commit}^{{tree}}')
            rc2, ls, _ = g('ls-tree', '-r', '-l', '--full-tree', commit, timeout=300)
            if rc != 0 or rc2 != 0:
                fails.append(f'{what}: {i}: commit {commit} has no readable tree')
                continue
            size = sum(int(f[3]) for f in (x.split(None, 4) for x in ls.splitlines())
                       if len(f) == 5 and f[3].isdigit())
            out[i] = {'dir': d, 'commit': commit, 'tree': tree.strip(), 'url': url,
                      'stage': src[i][0], 'path': src[i][1], 'size': size, 'name': name}
    return fails, out, covered


def inside_checkout(path):
    """PATH relative to the checkout when it lies inside it, else None."""
    rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.realpath(path), os.path.realpath(REPO))
    return None if rel == os.pardir or rel.startswith(os.pardir + os.sep) else rel


def checkout_state(work, adir=None):
    """(HEAD, the tree of the checkout as it is, clean): the tree holds the tracked files
    and the untracked ones git doesn't ignore (what a stage's COPY can read), written
    with a throwaway index. clean = that tree is HEAD's. ('', '', '') outside git. The
    artifacts folder ADIR is left out when it lies in the checkout (preflight requires
    git to ignore it; this keeps the exports out of .git even so)."""
    rc, head, _ = run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', 'HEAD'], 30)
    rc2, idx, _ = run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'rev-parse', '--path-format=absolute', '--git-path', 'index'], 30)
    if rc != 0 or rc2 != 0:
        return '', '', ''
    tmp = os.path.join(work, f'index.{time.monotonic_ns()}')
    if os.path.isfile(idx.strip()):
        shutil.copyfile(idx.strip(), tmp)
    env = {**os.environ, 'GIT_INDEX_FILE': tmp}
    spec = ['.']
    rel = inside_checkout(adir) if adir else None
    # an ignored folder is skipped by add -A already (and naming it errors)
    if rel not in (None, '.') and run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'check-ignore', '-q', rel], 30)[0] != 0:
        spec.append(f':(exclude){rel}')
    rc, _, _ = run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'add', '-A', '--ignore-errors', '--'] + spec, 120, env=env)
    rc3, tree, _ = run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'write-tree'], 60, env=env)
    rc4, htree, _ = run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'rev-parse', 'HEAD^{tree}'], 30)
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        os.remove(tmp)
    if rc != 0 or rc3 != 0 or rc4 != 0:
        return head.strip(), '', ''
    return head.strip(), tree.strip(), 'yes' if tree.strip() == htree.strip() else 'no'


def preflight(o, target, adir, work, log):
    """FR-004. Returns (failures, facts): facts hold what the build needs. Every check
    runs; an exception in one is that check's failure."""
    fails = []
    facts = {'arch': '', 'info': {}, 'over': {}, 'state': ('', '', ''), 'local': {}}
    dockerfile = os.path.join(REPO, 'Dockerfile')
    stages_dir = os.path.join(REPO, 'stages')

    def guard(what, fn, *a):
        try:
            return fn(*a)
        except Exception as e:      # noqa: BLE001 -- every failure is named, none ends preflight
            fails.append(f'{what}: {e}' if isinstance(e, (Fail, materialize.Fail))
                         else f'{what}: {type(e).__name__}: {e}')
            return None

    for tool in ('docker', 'git', 'python3'):
        if not shutil.which(tool):
            fails.append(f'{tool} not found')
    if fails:
        return fails, facts
    tfile = os.path.join(REPO, 'targets', target, 'target')
    if not materialize.NAME.fullmatch(target) or target.startswith('.') or not os.path.isfile(tfile):
        return [f'no target {target!r} (no {tfile})'], facts
    trec = guard(f'target {target}', materialize.record, tfile) or {}
    arch = trec.get('arch', '')
    if trec and not re.fullmatch(r'[a-z0-9]+', arch):
        fails.append(f'{tfile}: no arch')
    facts['arch'] = arch

    # the checkout this build is made from (compared again after the exports)
    rel = inside_checkout(adir)
    if rel is not None:
        if rel == '.':
            fails.append(f'--artifacts {adir}: the checkout itself; use a folder git ignores')
        elif run(['git', '-C', REPO, 'check-ignore', '-q', rel], 30)[0] != 0:
            fails.append(f'--artifacts {adir}: inside the checkout and not ignored by git '
                         '(the build would read it as an uncommitted change); add it to '
                         '.gitignore or use a folder outside the checkout')
    facts['state'] = guard('the checkout', checkout_state, work, adir) or ('', '', '')

    # the overrides, the pins and the locks
    over = {k: v for k, v in o['args'].items() if k != 'DEVICE'}
    over['DEVICE'] = target
    facts['over'] = {k: v for k, v in o['args'].items() if k != 'DEVICE'}

    # local checkouts: their commits are the inputs' commits from here on
    covered = set()
    if o['local']:
        def local():
            lf, li, cov = local_inputs(dockerfile, o['local'], dict(facts['over']))
            fails.extend(lf)
            covered.update(cov)
            return li
        facts['local'] = guard('--local', local) or {}
        for i, f in facts['local'].items():
            over[i] = facts['over'][i] = f['commit']
            log(f'preflight: {i} from the local checkout of {f["name"]}: {f["commit"]} (tree {f["tree"][:12]})')

    def pins_checks():
        declared = {w.split('=', 1)[0] for line in re.findall(r'^\s*ARG\s+(.+)$', glassine_pins._text(dockerfile), re.M)
                    for w in line.split()}
        for k in o['args']:
            if k == 'DEVICE':
                fails.append('--build-arg DEVICE: the target sets DEVICE')
            elif k not in declared:
                fails.append(f'--build-arg {k}: not an ARG of the Dockerfile')
        args, _ = glassine_pins.pins(dockerfile, over)
        # the target names its kernel stage; the Dockerfile's KERNEL (a pin) must be it
        if trec.get('kernel') and args.get('KERNEL') != trec['kernel']:
            fails.append(f'{tfile} names kernel={trec["kernel"]}, the build would use KERNEL={args.get("KERNEL")} '
                         f'(pin it in the Dockerfile, or --build-arg KERNEL={trec["kernel"]} for a trial)')
        st = glassine_pins.stages(dockerfile, args)
        chain = glassine_pins.chain(dockerfile, target, over)
        first_parent = st[chain[0]][0]
        if first_parent != 'scratch' and not re.search(r'[:@/]', first_parent):
            fails.append(f'the base chain of {target} starts from {first_parent!r}: no such stage '
                         f'(expected one stage per device, device-{target})')
        for name in glassine_pins.reachable(dockerfile, [BASE_EXPORT] + KERNEL_EXPORTS, over):
            sd = os.path.join(stages_dir, name)
            if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(sd, 'packages')) and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(sd, 'lock')):
                fails.append(f'stage {name}: no lock (stages/{name}/lock; scripts/lock.sh writes it)')
        return args
    args = guard('the Dockerfile', pins_checks) or {}

    # the parent (materialize checks it again; here it fails before any stage builds)
    if not o['no_parent']:
        def parent():
            with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):     # materialize says it again
                p = materialize.pick_parent(adir, target, o['parent'], False)
            log(f'preflight: parent {p or "none (no earlier build of " + target + ")"}')
        guard('parent', parent)

    # the git inputs: (url, commit) → the inputs and branches it serves
    branches = guard('the git inputs', glassine_pins.branches, dockerfile) or {}
    repo_args = guard('the git inputs', glassine_pins.repos, dockerfile) or {}
    fetches = {}
    lfetches = {}
    for i, b in branches.items():
        if i in facts['local']:
            lfetches.setdefault((facts['local'][i]['url'], facts['local'][i]['commit']), []).append((i, b))
        elif i in repo_args and i not in covered:
            fetches.setdefault((args.get(repo_args[i], ''), args.get(i, '')), []).append((i, b))
    builders = guard('the builder images', glassine_pins.builders, dockerfile, over) or {}
    others = guard('the platforms', glassine_pins.platforms, dockerfile) or []
    image = os.environ.get('MATERIALIZE_IMAGE', 'alpine:3.24')
    bt = os.environ.get('BUILD_TIMEOUT', '14400')
    if not bt.isdigit() or int(bt) == 0:
        fails.append(f'BUILD_TIMEOUT={bt!r}: not a number of seconds')

    # the slow checks, side by side
    os.makedirs(work, exist_ok=True)
    info = facts['info']
    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=8) as ex:
        f_emu = ex.submit(check_emulation, arch, others) if arch else None
        f_priv = ex.submit(check_privileged, image)
        f_git = {key: ex.submit(check_git, work, n, key[0], key[1], sorted({b for _, b in v}), log)
                 for n, (key, v) in enumerate(fetches.items())}
        f_loc = {key: ex.submit(check_git, work, len(fetches) + n, key[0], key[1],
                                sorted({b for _, b in v}), log, True)
                 for n, (key, v) in enumerate(lfetches.items())}
        imgs = [f'{im}@{dg}' for im, dg in builders.items()]
        if args.get('ALPINE'):
            imgs.append(args['ALPINE'])
        f_img = {r: ex.submit(check_image, r) for r in imgs}
        if f_emu:
            fails += guard('emulation', f_emu.result) or []
        pf, docker_df = guard('privileged container', f_priv.result) or ([], None)
        fails += pf
        copies = {(f['dir'], f['commit'], f['path']): f['size'] for f in facts['local'].values()}
        fails += guard('free space', check_space, adir, docker_df, int(1.5 * sum(copies.values()))) or []
        unmerged = []
        for key, fut in f_git.items():
            names = ' '.join(i for i, _ in fetches[key])
            gf, tree, merged = guard(names, fut.result) or (['no answer'], '', {})
            bad = set()
            for x in gf:
                b, msg = x if isinstance(x, tuple) else (None, x)
                who = [i for i, ib in fetches[key] if b is None or ib == b]
                bad |= set(who)
                fails.append(f'{" ".join(who)}: {msg}')
            for i, b in fetches[key]:
                info[f'input.{i}.tree'] = tree
                info[f'input.{i}.local'] = 'no'
                if i not in bad and not merged.get(b):
                    unmerged.append(i)
        for key, fut in f_loc.items():
            names = ' '.join(i for i, _ in lfetches[key])
            gf, _, merged = guard(names, fut.result) or (['no answer'], None, {})
            bad = set()
            for x in gf:
                b, msg = x if isinstance(x, tuple) else (None, x)
                who = [i for i, ib in lfetches[key] if b is None or ib == b]
                bad |= set(who)
                fails.append(f'{" ".join(who)}: {msg}')
            for i, b in lfetches[key]:
                info[f'input.{i}.tree'] = facts['local'][i]['tree']
                info[f'input.{i}.local'] = 'yes'
                if i not in bad and not merged.get(b):
                    unmerged.append(i)
        info['unmerged'] = ' '.join(i for i in branches if i in unmerged)
        for r, f in f_img.items():
            fails += guard(f'image {r}', f.result) or []
    for im, dg in builders.items():
        info[f'builder.{im}'] = dg
    head, _, clean = facts['state']
    info['images_commit'], info['images_clean'] = head, clean
    return fails, facts


# ---- the build ---------------------------------------------------------------------

class Log:
    def __init__(self, path):
        self.f = open(path, 'a', buffering=1)

    def __call__(self, msg, show=True):
        if show:
            print(msg, flush=True)
        self.f.write(msg + '\n')

    def stream(self, cmd, timeout, show=False):
        """Run cmd in its own process group, its output into the log (and to the screen
        when show); returns (returncode, output). Killed after timeout seconds (124), and
        stopped when this command ends any other way (a signal, an exception)."""
        self.f.write('$ ' + ' '.join(cmd) + '\n')
        out = []
        p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True,
                             errors='replace', bufsize=1, start_new_session=True)
        t_end = time.monotonic() + timeout
        timed_out = False
        try:
            sel = selectors.DefaultSelector()
            sel.register(p.stdout, selectors.EVENT_READ)
            while True:
                left = t_end - time.monotonic()
                if left <= 0:
                    timed_out = True
                    break
                if not sel.select(timeout=min(left, 5)):
                    continue
                line = p.stdout.readline()
                if not line:
                    break
                out.append(line)
                self.f.write(line)
                if show:
                    sys.stdout.write(line)
                    sys.stdout.flush()
        except BaseException:
            stop(p)
            raise
        if timed_out:
            stop(p)
        p.wait()
        if timed_out:
            self.f.write(f'timed out after {timeout} s\n')
            return 124, ''.join(out)
        return p.returncode, ''.join(out)


def stop(p, grace=15):
    """Stop a child's process group: SIGINT (docker buildx cancels the build, materialize
    cleans its staging), then SIGKILL after grace seconds."""
    for sig, wait in ((signal.SIGINT, grace), (signal.SIGKILL, 5)):
        with contextlib.suppress(ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
            os.killpg(p.pid, sig)
        try:
            p.wait(timeout=wait)
            return
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            pass


def prepare_local(root, src, commit, path, log):
    """commit of the checkout src in root/<path>, the way a source stage fetches its
    pinned commit: a fresh repository with that one commit (shallow), checked out. None
    when done, else why not."""
    d = root + path
    os.makedirs(d)

    def g(*a, timeout=60):
        return run(['git', '-C', d, '-c', 'advice.detachedHead=false', *a], timeout,
                   env={**os.environ, 'GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT': '0'})
    for a, tmo in ((('init', '-q'), 60),
                   (('fetch', '-q', '--depth=1', 'file://' + src, commit), 1800),
                   (('checkout', '-q', 'FETCH_HEAD'), 1800)):
        rc, out, err = g(*a, timeout=tmo)
        if rc != 0:
            return f'git {a[0]} failed: {last(err) or last(out)}'
    rc, head, _ = g('rev-parse', 'HEAD')
    rc2, st, _ = g('status', '--porcelain', timeout=600)
    if rc != 0 or head.strip() != commit or rc2 != 0 or st.strip():
        return f'the copy is not {commit} unchanged'
    log(f'build: local checkout {commit[:12]} ready')
    return None


def clear_stale(adir):
    """Remove .work-<pid> directories of runs that ended without cleaning up (killed):
    only that name, and only when no process has that pid."""
    for n in os.listdir(adir):
        m = re.fullmatch(r'\.work-(\d+)', n)
        if not m or int(m.group(1)) == os.getpid():
            continue
        try:
            os.kill(int(m.group(1)), 0)
            continue                    # alive (ours or not): leave it
        except ProcessLookupError:
            pass
        except PermissionError:
            continue
        shutil.rmtree(os.path.join(adir, n), ignore_errors=True)


def on_signal(signum, frame):
    raise SystemExit(128 + signum)


def tail(text, n=15):
    return '\n'.join('    ' + x for x in text.rstrip().splitlines()[-n:])


def main(argv):
    sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)
    o, target = parse(argv)
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    start = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).replace(tzinfo=None, microsecond=0)
    adir = os.path.abspath(o['artifacts'])
    os.makedirs(adir, exist_ok=True)
    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(sig, on_signal)
    clear_stale(adir)
    work = os.path.join(adir, f'.work-{os.getpid()}')
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    os.makedirs(work)
    logdir = os.path.join(adir, '.logs', target if materialize.NAME.fullmatch(target) else '_')
    os.makedirs(logdir, exist_ok=True)
    logpath = os.path.join(logdir, f'{start:%Y%m%d-%H%M%S}.log')
    log = Log(logpath)
    times = []

    def step(name, t):
        times.append((name, time.monotonic() - t))
        log(f'time {name:<26} {times[-1][1]:6.2f} s')

    try:
        log(f'build: {target} into {adir}, log {logpath}')
        t = time.monotonic()
        try:
            fails, facts = preflight(o, target, adir, work, log)
        except Exception as e:      # noqa: BLE001 -- preflight's own guard missed it
            fails, facts = [f'preflight: {type(e).__name__}: {e}'], {}
        step('preflight', t)
        if fails:
            for f in fails:
                log(f'preflight: FAIL: {f}')
            return 3
        log('preflight: ok')
        info = facts['info']
        if o['preflight_only']:
            for k in sorted(info):
                log(f'{k}={info[k]}')
            return 0
        over = facts['over']
        plat = f'linux/{facts["arch"]}'
        timeout = int(os.environ.get('BUILD_TIMEOUT', 14400))
        common = ['docker', 'buildx', 'build', '--progress=plain', '--platform', plat,
                  '--build-arg', f'DEVICE={target}']
        for k, v in over.items():
            common += ['--build-arg', f'{k}={v}']

        # the local checkouts: each commit in a fresh shallow checkout, the source stage's
        # build context (an input following another at the same commit shares its copy)
        contexts = {}
        if facts['local']:
            t = time.monotonic()
            copies = {}
            for i, f in facts['local'].items():
                key = (f['dir'], f['commit'], f['path'])
                if key not in copies:
                    root = os.path.join(work, 'local', str(len(copies)))
                    why = prepare_local(root, *key, log)
                    if why:
                        log(f'build: the local checkout for {i}: {why}')
                        return 1
                    copies[key] = root
                contexts[f['stage']] = copies[key]
            for stage, root in sorted(contexts.items()):
                common += ['--build-context', f'{stage}={root}']
            step('local checkouts', t)

        # the exports. Without cache, each stage is built once in this run: an export
        # rebuilds only the stages no earlier export of this run built
        tar = os.path.join(work, 'base.tar')
        kdir = os.path.join(work, 'k')
        dockerfile = os.path.join(REPO, 'Dockerfile')
        built = set()
        for name in [BASE_EXPORT] + KERNEL_EXPORTS:
            dest = (f'type=tar,dest={tar}' if name == BASE_EXPORT
                    else f'type=local,dest={os.path.join(work, "k." + name)}')
            extra = []
            if o['no_cache']:
                need = glassine_pins.reachable(dockerfile, [name], {**over, 'DEVICE': target})
                fresh = [n for n in need if n not in built and n not in contexts]
                built.update(need)
                if fresh:
                    extra = ['--no-cache-filter', ','.join(fresh)]
            log(f'build: {name} ...')
            t = time.monotonic()
            rc, out = log.stream(common + extra + ['--target', name, '-o', dest, REPO], timeout)
            if rc != 0:
                log(f'build: {name} failed (exit {rc}{", timeout" if rc == 124 else ""}):\n{tail(out)}')
                return 1
            step(f'export {name}', t)
        os.makedirs(kdir)
        for name in KERNEL_EXPORTS:
            src = os.path.join(work, 'k.' + name)
            rc, out = log.stream(['cp', '-a', src + '/.', kdir + '/'], 600)
            if rc != 0:
                log(f'build: merging {name} failed:\n{tail(out)}')
                return 1
            shutil.rmtree(src)

        # the checks
        t = time.monotonic()
        kargs = [x for k, v in over.items() for x in ('--arg', f'{k}={v}')]
        # the boot image of a build that sets CMDLINE_EXTRA is checked with those words;
        # any other must carry no glassine.devmode
        bargs = ['--cmdline-extra', over['CMDLINE_EXTRA']] if over.get('CMDLINE_EXTRA', '').strip() else []
        for cmd in ([sys.executable, os.path.join(HERE, 'kernel-check')] + kargs + [kdir],
                    [sys.executable, os.path.join(HERE, 'boot-check'), kdir, target] + bargs):
            rc, out = log.stream(cmd, 600)
            if rc != 0:
                log(f'build: {os.path.basename(cmd[1])} failed:\n{tail(out)}')
                return 1
            log(f'build: {os.path.basename(cmd[1])}: {last(out)}')
        step('kernel-check, boot-check', t)

        # the build info: the checkout must still be the one preflight saw, since the
        # exports read it one after another and the record names its commit
        now = checkout_state(work, adir)
        if now != facts['state']:
            log(f'build: the checkout changed during the build (commit {facts["state"][0][:12] or "?"} '
                f'→ {now[0][:12] or "?"}, tree {facts["state"][1][:12] or "?"} → {now[1][:12] or "?"}); '
                f'nothing recorded, build again')
            return 1
        bi = os.path.join(work, 'build-info')
        with open(bi, 'w') as f:
            f.write(''.join(f'{k}={info[k]}\n' for k in sorted(info)))

        # materialize
        t = time.monotonic()
        cmd = [sys.executable, os.path.join(HERE, 'materialize'), '--build-info', bi,
               '--time', f'{start:%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ}']
        cmd += [x for k, v in over.items() for x in ('--arg', f'{k}={v}')]
        if o['no_parent']:
            cmd.append('--no-parent')
        elif o['parent']:
            cmd += ['--parent', o['parent']]
        cmd += [tar, kdir, target, adir]
        rc, out = log.stream(cmd, timeout, show=True)
        if rc == 4:
            log('build: another materialization holds the host lock; run again when it is done')
            return 4
        if rc != 0:
            log(f'build: materialize failed (exit {rc})')
            return 1
        step('materialize', t)
        times.append(('total', time.monotonic() - t0))
        m = re.search(r'^materialize: build \S+/builds/(\S+): base (\S+) \((new|reused)\)', out, re.M)
        log('')
        if m:
            log(f'build {m.group(1)}: base {m.group(2)} ({m.group(3)})')
        for name, s in times:
            log(f'  {name:<28} {s:7.1f} s')
        return 0
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    try:
        sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        sys.exit(130)
